cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cross-scale organisation of the atmospheric circulation: a falsification-grade research programme (Shroedinger, gen4)"
version: "5.0"
type: software
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/Shroedinger"
url: "https://github.com/Theclimateguy/Shroedinger"
date-released: 2026-08-16
authors:
  - family-names: "Sotiriadi"
    given-names: "N."
abstract: >-
  Preregistered research programme on the cross-scale organisation of the
  atmospheric circulation. The surviving invariant is the envelope-coupling
  profile P: the spatial rank correlation between activity maps of adjacent
  octave levels of the 850 hPa relative vorticity field. P forms a season-,
  year- and ENSO-stable regional signature (p = 0.001 on held-out samples),
  replicates in an independent reanalysis, and - decisively - replicates in a
  free-running CMIP6 HighResMIP integration that assimilates no atmospheric
  observations (rho = 0.71 against an ERA5-to-ERA5 ceiling of 0.93), which
  closes the observing-network confound. The interpretation of the
  inter-level transfer asymmetry index A is retracted: A is a reproducible
  regional statistic but responds to temporal persistence rather than to
  cross-level irrecoverability. Three derived applied predictions were tested
  and failed. The repository contains fourteen frozen protocols with
  deviation logs, the full experiment catalogue, numerical results and the
  complete catalogue of negative results.
keywords:
  - hierarchical organisation of geosystems
  - invariants
  - scale
  - atmospheric dynamics
  - ERA5
  - MERRA-2
  - regionalisation
  - downscaling
  - preregistration
  - negative results
